{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent underprediction in rising regimes: when the last 5–10 days show an upswing/acceleration, add an upward bias to the forecast path (model is ~1–3 EUR too low for much of the first ~15–20 days).",
    "Trend/level lag: the forecast reacts too slowly to regime shifts (especially rallies). Heuristic: if spot is above the 20–30d mean and the mean is rising, shift the whole forecast level up (reduce smoothing/lag).",
    "Peak/volatility underestimation: the model misses sharp upside spikes (e.g., true jumps to 72–73 while forecast stays ~69–71). Heuristic: increase amplitude during high momentum/large prior daily moves (widen forecast range upward).",
    "Late-horizon downside overshoot: beyond ~day 20, the model tends to drift too low vs realized levels (except when a genuine selloff occurs). Heuristic: dampen late-horizon downward drift; pull tail forecasts toward the recent mean unless strong negative momentum is present.",
    "Selloff timing mismatch: when a real late drop happens (e.g., true falls to ~65), the model often predicts it earlier/higher and then fails to match the exact timing. Heuristic: delay mean-reversion/selloff calls unless confirmed by consecutive down days; otherwise keep forecasts closer to current level."
  ]
}
